libportal: notification media without memfd_create on QNX.

The notification portal v2 code passes icons/sounds as memfd_create(...,
MFD_ALLOW_SEALING) file descriptors. QNX has neither memfd_create() nor file
seals, so the build fails ('MFD_ALLOW_SEALING' undeclared, implicit
memfd_create). Where MFD_ALLOW_SEALING is not defined, create the buffer as an
unlinked temporary file instead: it is anonymous, can be passed over D-Bus,
truncated, mmap'ed and written like a memfd, only without seals (the code
never adds any). Linux keeps the memfd path unchanged.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/libportal/notification.c
+++ b/libportal/notification.c
@@ -35,6 +35,24 @@
 #include "notification.h"
 #include "portal-private.h"
 
+#ifndef MFD_ALLOW_SEALING
+/* No memfd_create() (QNX): an unlinked temporary file gives the same
+ * anonymous, fd-passable, mmap-able and writable buffer, without seals. */
+#define MFD_ALLOW_SEALING 0
+static int
+xdp_memfd_create (const char *name, unsigned int flags)
+{
+  g_autofree char *tmpl = g_build_filename (g_get_tmp_dir (), "libportal-XXXXXX", NULL);
+  int fd;
+
+  fd = g_mkstemp_full (tmpl, O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC, 0600);
+  if (fd != -1)
+    g_unlink (tmpl);
+  return fd;
+}
+#define memfd_create(name, flags) xdp_memfd_create (name, flags)
+#endif
+
 static void
 action_invoked (GDBusConnection *bus,
                 const char *sender_name,
